  "notes": "Pinterest API v5 is REST, OAuth 2.0 only (Authorization Code, Client Credentials, Refresh Token grants); token exchange uses HTTP Basic with client_id/client_secret, API calls use Bearer token. New apps must first be approved for free Trial access (sandbox-only Pins/Boards, business-day approval per community reports), then separately apply and wait 1-4 weeks with a demo video for Standard access to unlock full functionality/rate limits — this two-stage review gates real production use, hence admin_approval/app_review rather than self-serve. No official Pinterest-published MCP server found; only community MCP servers (e.g. cesteral/pinterest-mcp, getmcpads pinterest-ads) exist per registry hints.",
